WEBVTT

00:00:09.530 --> 00:00:11.160
My vision...

00:00:11.160 --> 00:00:13.240
It's all one big blur.

00:00:13.240 --> 00:00:15.870
I feel... sick.

00:00:19.460 --> 00:00:23.340
Noé, fall back!
Don't try to fight like that!

00:00:23.340 --> 00:00:27.800
Huh? There is no way I'm leaving you here.

00:00:27.800 --> 00:00:30.050
You're in no shape to worry about me!

00:00:30.050 --> 00:00:32.680
You didn't heed my warning, you fool!

00:00:32.680 --> 00:00:36.180
Every time you open your mouth,
it's impossible to follow.

00:00:36.180 --> 00:00:39.270
It's always the same
old story with you, Vanitas!

00:00:39.270 --> 00:00:43.020
One moment. What did you just say?

00:00:46.190 --> 00:00:48.610
Vanitas?

00:00:48.610 --> 00:00:52.610
Black hair and blue eyes.

00:00:52.610 --> 00:00:54.240
Dear Vanitas?

00:00:54.240 --> 00:00:55.280
What?

00:00:55.280 --> 00:00:58.250
You're the one they call Vanitas?!

00:00:58.250 --> 00:01:00.870
What the--?! Yes, it's me!

00:01:03.040 --> 00:01:04.420
Dear God!

00:01:04.420 --> 00:01:08.960
O Lord, I give thanks
for Thy guiding hand!

00:01:08.960 --> 00:01:13.590
To think we'd meet so soon!

00:01:13.590 --> 00:01:18.100
So the rumors about you
being used by vampires were true!

00:01:18.100 --> 00:01:18.930
Huh?!

00:01:18.930 --> 00:01:21.390
Did they coerce you into cooperating?

00:01:21.390 --> 00:01:23.650
Are they holding a loved one hostage?!

00:01:23.650 --> 00:01:24.520
Get off me!

00:01:24.520 --> 00:01:30.070
This poor boy was forced to dwell
among vampires and the Blue Moon Clan.

00:01:30.070 --> 00:01:37.030
What a pitiful creature.

00:01:37.030 --> 00:01:39.950
You people will never change.

00:01:39.950 --> 00:01:44.580
You cast pity where it's unwanted.
You don't realize you look down on others.

00:01:44.580 --> 00:01:49.250
Listen here! I choose my
own path no matter what I do!

00:01:49.250 --> 00:01:51.420
I consort with vampires.

00:01:51.420 --> 00:01:53.630
I snuck into your lair.

00:01:53.630 --> 00:01:57.260
And I just raked your face.

00:01:57.260 --> 00:01:59.680
It was all of my own free will!

00:01:59.680 --> 00:02:04.440
You fools may be slaves to
this god of yours, but not me!

00:02:12.690 --> 00:02:15.410
You poor thing.

00:02:32.210 --> 00:02:37.260
<i>You're pondering the simple things,</i>
<i>pretty much: human emotions, and love?</i>

00:02:37.260 --> 00:02:41.640
<i>I hope one day you'll understand</i>

00:02:41.640 --> 00:02:46.230
<i>Too many wounds have left you</i>
<i>patched together, a miserable sight</i>

00:02:46.230 --> 00:02:51.480
<i>That doesn't even know</i>
<i>the definition of "alive"</i>

00:02:51.480 --> 00:02:58.990
<i>No need to say,</i>
<i>"Just the two of us" or anything</i>

00:02:58.990 --> 00:03:07.580
<i>I've a feeling we can understand</i>
<i>each other, and that's fine for now</i>

00:03:09.080 --> 00:03:16.550
<i>I love this world,</i>
<i>and the light only you give me</i>

00:03:16.550 --> 00:03:21.430
<i>Makes the world I see</i>
<i>through these fractured eyes </i>

00:03:21.430 --> 00:03:26.100
<i>Look gleaming and bright</i>

00:03:26.100 --> 00:03:30.690
<i>There's no such thing as a sure thing</i>

00:03:30.690 --> 00:03:35.440
<i>But you can see me, can't you?</i>

00:03:38.950 --> 00:03:44.290
<i>When sky and void meet, look back</i>
<i>because the dreams will come later</i>

00:03:49.000 --> 00:03:53.300
O Lord, I beseech Thee!
Have mercy upon him!

00:03:53.300 --> 00:03:59.300
Surely he knows not what he does.

00:04:01.390 --> 00:04:03.720
Open your eyes, Dear Vanitas.

00:04:03.720 --> 00:04:09.350
The Word of God shall not reach your
soul if you turn your back on His light!

00:04:09.350 --> 00:04:12.770
Forget your god for now and listen to me!

00:04:12.770 --> 00:04:14.860
Look at me!

00:04:14.860 --> 00:04:18.610
I want you to know God's love through me!

00:04:18.610 --> 00:04:19.530
Huh?

00:04:19.530 --> 00:04:22.620
It's all right. There is nothing to fear.

00:04:22.620 --> 00:04:28.660
Though you have gone astray,
the Lord will never abandon you!

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:34.960
I shall not fail to save you
from the vampires' evil clutches.

00:04:34.960 --> 00:04:37.340
You're creeping me out!

00:04:42.510 --> 00:04:45.470
My vision's coming back.

00:04:45.470 --> 00:04:47.100
Now I can do something.

00:04:47.100 --> 00:04:49.270
It is time, Durandal!

00:04:49.270 --> 00:04:50.270
Noé!

00:04:51.650 --> 00:04:52.480
He's swift!

00:04:52.480 --> 00:04:54.900
Chasseurs are no mere humans!

00:04:54.900 --> 00:04:57.650
They use drugs to enhance
their combat prowess!

00:04:57.650 --> 00:05:00.650
That explains it!
You could have told me sooner!

00:05:00.650 --> 00:05:02.780
Will you ever learn?!

00:05:12.830 --> 00:05:14.040
Impressive.

00:05:14.040 --> 00:05:19.550
I've never seen a vampire move so
swiftly after being struck by that light.

00:05:19.550 --> 00:05:21.880
Please, wait! Listen to me!

00:05:21.880 --> 00:05:23.260
I already told you.

00:05:23.260 --> 00:05:28.180
No vampire who sets foot
in here leaves this place alive.

00:05:28.180 --> 00:05:30.480
Big city vampires never listen.

00:05:30.480 --> 00:05:33.480
And you humans are no different!

00:05:34.940 --> 00:05:39.730
I didn't see a lever
on the wall out there.

00:05:39.730 --> 00:05:42.110
That means...

00:05:42.110 --> 00:05:43.820
There!

00:05:47.160 --> 00:05:49.290
I'm at a disadvantage here.

00:05:49.290 --> 00:05:53.330
If I keep my distance and
wait for my strength to recover...

00:05:53.330 --> 00:05:54.750
Trying to escape?

00:05:54.750 --> 00:05:56.880
You coward!

00:06:00.010 --> 00:06:02.670
You're not going anywhere...

00:06:02.670 --> 00:06:04.720
...vampire!

00:06:21.990 --> 00:06:24.740
If I deny him his weapon...!

00:06:36.040 --> 00:06:38.920
What... in the devil... was that?

00:06:38.920 --> 00:06:40.630
This ends now!

00:06:41.670 --> 00:06:43.300
What the...?!

00:06:51.600 --> 00:06:53.930
Ow, ow, ow...

00:06:57.480 --> 00:06:59.940
They got away.

00:06:59.940 --> 00:07:01.110
Captain!

00:07:01.110 --> 00:07:03.150
Ah, Maria, Georges.

00:07:03.150 --> 00:07:06.610
Oh, no! You're bleeding!

00:07:06.610 --> 00:07:12.950
Excellent timing. I got lost and
then ran into a pair of intruders.

00:07:12.950 --> 00:07:16.330
One of them was a vampire.

00:07:18.630 --> 00:07:21.040
Now then...

00:07:21.040 --> 00:07:22.840
The hunt is on.

00:07:24.050 --> 00:07:25.970
Dear Vanitas!

00:07:25.970 --> 00:07:29.430
Where are you? Come out,
come out wherever you are!

00:07:29.430 --> 00:07:32.510
Please, Captain. Lower your voice.

00:07:32.510 --> 00:07:36.350
But Dear Vanitas might heed my call.

00:07:36.350 --> 00:07:38.850
He's not going to answer!

00:07:38.850 --> 00:07:40.230
Dear Vanitas!

00:07:40.230 --> 00:07:41.520
Enough! Be silent!

00:07:41.520 --> 00:07:43.940
He really does creep me out!

00:07:43.940 --> 00:07:46.240
That Roland fellow...

00:07:46.240 --> 00:07:50.070
You saw it didn't you?
Those eyes brimming with goodwill?

00:07:50.070 --> 00:07:56.500
Such sanctimonious fools who won't accept
malice for what it is are the worst!

00:07:56.500 --> 00:08:02.130
They twist every provocation and
rejection to suit their own needs.

00:08:06.420 --> 00:08:09.130
Oh, forgive me.

00:08:09.130 --> 00:08:13.510
I never thought that
you'd meet your match.

00:08:13.510 --> 00:08:18.350
But I don't see the problem.
I've grown rather fond of him.

00:08:18.350 --> 00:08:21.770
Whatever you say, Mr. Personality.

00:08:24.570 --> 00:08:26.070
How are your eyes?

00:08:26.070 --> 00:08:28.950
Much better now.

00:08:28.950 --> 00:08:33.410
But the real and formulaic worlds
are still a mixed-up, sickening blur.

00:08:33.410 --> 00:08:37.870
That light likely hinders the
function of a vampire's eyes,

00:08:37.870 --> 00:08:41.210
thus preventing the
rewriting of the World Formula.

00:08:41.210 --> 00:08:45.130
Noé, you enhance your body in combat.

00:08:45.130 --> 00:08:49.260
What else can you do by
tampering with the World Formula?

00:08:49.260 --> 00:08:53.390
If I try hard enough,
I can stand on a wall or ceiling.

00:08:55.640 --> 00:08:58.270
Do you think you can defeat him?

00:09:06.070 --> 00:09:08.860
I don't know, but...

00:09:08.860 --> 00:09:12.410
We can win... if we work together.

00:09:24.880 --> 00:09:29.300
Noé, I came here looking for someone.

00:09:29.300 --> 00:09:31.260
His name is Moreau.

00:09:31.260 --> 00:09:33.430
He was obsessed with vampire research.

00:09:33.430 --> 00:09:37.810
His madness got him
expelled from the Chasseurs.

00:09:37.810 --> 00:09:39.350
Look at this.

00:09:39.350 --> 00:09:42.480
The button Dante took from that abductor?

00:09:42.480 --> 00:09:44.730
Look at the other side.

00:09:46.650 --> 00:09:49.320
Number 128?

00:09:49.320 --> 00:09:51.950
It's a production number.

00:09:51.950 --> 00:09:58.450
The recent abductions weren't
the work of ordinary Chasseurs.

00:09:58.450 --> 00:10:03.040
They are enhanced humans,
the fruit of Moreau's human experiments.

00:10:03.040 --> 00:10:05.420
They're his creations.

00:10:11.340 --> 00:10:13.720
Now who do we have here?

00:10:13.720 --> 00:10:18.510
The black-haired one seems familiar,
or am I just imagining things?

00:10:21.470 --> 00:10:22.980
Vanitas?

00:10:22.980 --> 00:10:25.560
The Vampire of the Blue Moon?

00:10:25.560 --> 00:10:30.980
That black-haired, blue-eyed lad
went by such a name.

00:10:32.990 --> 00:10:36.490
Why, yes! Yes! I just remembered!

00:10:36.490 --> 00:10:39.450
It <i>is </i>him! The lad from back then!

00:10:39.450 --> 00:10:43.040
Welcome home! Welcome home! Welcome home!

00:10:43.040 --> 00:10:46.370
The Vampire of the Blue Moon
robbed him from me!

00:10:46.370 --> 00:10:50.340
He was my precious test subject!

00:10:59.140 --> 00:11:02.470
All right, let's go, Noé.

00:11:03.680 --> 00:11:06.560
I repeat, there are two intruders.

00:11:06.560 --> 00:11:09.730
A blonde-haired vampire
and a black-haired human.

00:11:09.730 --> 00:11:13.650
However, I want the
human taken alive at all costs.

00:11:13.650 --> 00:11:15.820
Do <i>not </i>slay him.

00:11:18.660 --> 00:11:21.620
To think two intruders
would trouble us so...

00:11:21.620 --> 00:11:24.330
Olivier will have my head for this.

00:11:24.330 --> 00:11:29.000
Captain, seeing as one of them
is Vanitas of the Blue Moon Clan,

00:11:29.000 --> 00:11:33.760
should we have not reported that fact?

00:11:33.760 --> 00:11:34.800
That's true!

00:11:34.800 --> 00:11:36.590
Seriously?!

00:11:37.590 --> 00:11:41.680
Oh, never mind.
I'll submit a full report later.

00:11:41.680 --> 00:11:43.680
Now, let us go!

00:11:43.680 --> 00:11:46.180
We have the home-field advantage!

00:11:46.180 --> 00:11:50.560
This place will be your grave, vampire!

00:11:50.560 --> 00:11:52.900
What the--?!

00:11:52.900 --> 00:11:56.490
The automatons are attacking us?!

00:11:58.490 --> 00:12:02.700
The astermite is glowing red.
I've never seen such a reaction.

00:12:02.700 --> 00:12:04.950
Snap out of it. What happened here?

00:12:04.950 --> 00:12:08.500
Captain, there's something
wrong with those two.

00:12:08.500 --> 00:12:12.460
It's as if they know this labyrinth
like the back of their hand.

00:12:12.460 --> 00:12:16.630
We were on their tail,
but they somehow circled behind us

00:12:16.630 --> 00:12:18.970
and took us by surprise!

00:12:18.970 --> 00:12:22.260
And that eldritch light...

00:12:22.260 --> 00:12:27.520
It was as if we, the Chasseurs,
had gone from hunters to prey.

00:12:32.770 --> 00:12:36.690
That book can even tamper with machines?

00:12:36.690 --> 00:12:38.320
Not exactly.

00:12:38.320 --> 00:12:42.820
It tampered with the astermite
powering the automatons.

00:12:42.820 --> 00:12:47.120
Surely you understand why that's possible?

00:12:47.120 --> 00:12:50.370
Don't tell me you rewrote its formula?!

00:12:50.370 --> 00:12:55.960
Precisely. That stone has a conduit to
the World Formula, just as vampires do.

00:12:55.960 --> 00:12:57.800
I simply used it.

00:12:57.800 --> 00:13:03.090
What a pain. I thought we'd reach
our goal without crossing the Chasseurs.

00:13:03.090 --> 00:13:05.350
Things never go as planned.

00:13:06.350 --> 00:13:08.770
I've so many other questions.

00:13:08.770 --> 00:13:14.110
How do you know this place so well
that you can bedevil the Chasseurs?

00:13:14.110 --> 00:13:17.190
What is that man Moreau trying to achieve?

00:13:17.190 --> 00:13:20.240
What is your connection to him?

00:13:20.240 --> 00:13:23.780
And why is it that at times...

00:13:25.870 --> 00:13:28.160
...you make that face?

00:13:28.160 --> 00:13:29.830
Hey.

00:13:29.830 --> 00:13:31.540
Quit making that face.

00:13:31.540 --> 00:13:33.880
I always look like this!

00:13:33.880 --> 00:13:36.500
Don't lie to me.

00:13:39.420 --> 00:13:41.970
My parents were slain by a vampire.

00:13:41.970 --> 00:13:43.010
What?

00:13:43.010 --> 00:13:46.350
The Chasseurs saved me from the same fate.

00:13:46.350 --> 00:13:51.060
And the Church began training me
to join them as a new recruit.

00:13:51.060 --> 00:13:54.020
But before I was ready,
Moreau took notice of me,

00:13:54.020 --> 00:13:57.570
and I became his guinea pig.

00:13:57.570 --> 00:13:59.860
End of story.

00:14:00.860 --> 00:14:04.530
End of... story?

00:14:04.530 --> 00:14:08.660
Oh, and I spent years down here,
so I know it well.

00:14:08.660 --> 00:14:10.540
It's as simple as that.

00:14:10.540 --> 00:14:13.920
That's not what I meant.

00:14:13.920 --> 00:14:17.920
Why did he tell that story
as if it were someone else?

00:14:19.210 --> 00:14:24.300
You don't hold a grudge against vampires?

00:14:24.300 --> 00:14:29.430
The way I see it, humans and
vampires are much the same.

00:14:29.430 --> 00:14:34.310
They're both truly monstrous
and endlessly selfish creatures.

00:14:38.270 --> 00:14:41.480
There it is again!
Please don't make that face!

00:14:41.480 --> 00:14:42.900
Keep your voice down!

00:14:42.900 --> 00:14:46.200
Seeing you make
that face raises my hackles!

00:14:46.200 --> 00:14:48.950
Yeah?! Well, sorry! I was born with it!

00:14:48.950 --> 00:14:51.040
No, you weren't, you liar!

00:14:51.040 --> 00:14:52.750
Why you...!

00:14:53.790 --> 00:14:56.420
There you are, Dear Vanitas!

00:14:57.830 --> 00:15:00.300
Noé! Close your eyes!

00:15:04.720 --> 00:15:06.300
The security gate!

00:15:07.340 --> 00:15:09.760
They will not escape! To the bypass!

00:15:09.760 --> 00:15:10.760
Wait, Maria!

00:15:10.760 --> 00:15:13.770
It's no use. The controls won't respond!

00:15:17.400 --> 00:15:20.320
Now, listen carefully, Noé.

00:15:20.320 --> 00:15:24.280
From this point, we have
to beat Roland without fighting.

00:15:24.280 --> 00:15:25.490
Without fighting?

00:15:25.490 --> 00:15:27.860
That's right. He's formidable.

00:15:27.860 --> 00:15:31.200
He may be one of the
mightiest of the Chasseurs.

00:15:31.200 --> 00:15:34.910
If we fight, we won't come out unscathed.

00:15:34.910 --> 00:15:41.090
We're now making our way toward Moreau,
along with his enhanced humans.

00:15:41.090 --> 00:15:46.420
The abducted vampires should
be there, too, if they yet live.

00:15:46.420 --> 00:15:49.260
We can't afford to get wounded here.

00:15:49.260 --> 00:15:52.100
This ends now.

00:15:57.850 --> 00:16:00.480
That's no way to treat a lady!

00:16:00.480 --> 00:16:03.360
A tasty little fly caught in our web.

00:16:03.360 --> 00:16:05.320
We're taking her hostage!

00:16:05.320 --> 00:16:06.530
Overruled!

00:16:06.530 --> 00:16:08.280
I overrule your overruling!

00:16:08.280 --> 00:16:10.030
Not this again?!

00:16:10.030 --> 00:16:13.450
This is the swiftest way
to deal with men like Roland!

00:16:13.450 --> 00:16:15.120
I'm against it!

00:16:15.120 --> 00:16:19.290
It will dash any hope
of a peaceful resolution!

00:16:19.290 --> 00:16:21.040
Huh?!

00:16:21.040 --> 00:16:25.460
How can you still think like that?!
There <i>is </i>no peaceful resolution with him!

00:16:25.460 --> 00:16:29.380
If we explain the situation and
clear up this misunderstanding--

00:16:29.380 --> 00:16:33.810
This is what makes you people weak!

00:16:33.810 --> 00:16:38.810
You have great power yet dig your
own graves by shackling yourselves.

00:16:38.810 --> 00:16:39.640
Vanitas--

00:16:39.640 --> 00:16:42.810
Enough! I'm done with you!

00:16:42.810 --> 00:16:47.240
If you don't like my way of doing things,
you're free to go it alone!

00:16:47.240 --> 00:16:53.780
Working with naive fools like you
will be the death of me someday!

00:16:53.780 --> 00:17:00.960
Go make nice with your preachy pals,
you candied-brained, blood-sucking bat!

00:17:03.290 --> 00:17:06.000
Message received, Vanitas.

00:17:06.000 --> 00:17:08.720
I take back what I said.

00:17:08.720 --> 00:17:12.180
We <i>are </i>going to take a hostage.

00:17:12.180 --> 00:17:13.430
What?

00:17:20.940 --> 00:17:22.150
Dear Vanitas!

00:17:22.150 --> 00:17:23.730
Stay right where you are.

00:17:23.730 --> 00:17:28.440
One false move and I'll snap
his bony neck in the wink of an eye.

00:17:28.440 --> 00:17:31.530
Hey, you're stealing... my lines.

00:17:31.530 --> 00:17:34.240
Foul vampire! How can you stoop so low?!

00:17:34.240 --> 00:17:38.160
Please calm yourself, Captain!
It may very well be a trap!

00:17:38.160 --> 00:17:40.330
Yes, but even so...!

00:17:40.330 --> 00:17:42.870
What's gotten into you, you fool?!

00:17:42.870 --> 00:17:44.540
He'll see through this act.

00:17:44.540 --> 00:17:48.590
Act? You say the silliest things, Vanitas.

00:17:48.590 --> 00:17:49.210
Huh?

00:17:49.210 --> 00:17:51.130
Did I not tell you before?

00:17:51.130 --> 00:17:52.050
What?

00:17:52.050 --> 00:17:55.100
We can win if we work together.

00:17:55.100 --> 00:17:56.930
Those are some scary eyes!

00:17:56.930 --> 00:17:59.720
Don't just stand there, Roland!

00:17:59.720 --> 00:18:01.560
Hurry up and save me!

00:18:01.560 --> 00:18:04.310
I'm serious! Please save me!

00:18:04.310 --> 00:18:07.610
Are you saying it's all an act, Georges?

00:18:07.610 --> 00:18:09.530
It's so hard to tell.

00:18:09.530 --> 00:18:15.280
Vanitas, there is one thing
you said earlier that I agree with.

00:18:15.280 --> 00:18:18.740
We must not let him deal the first blow.

00:18:18.740 --> 00:18:20.000
With that in mind!

00:18:20.000 --> 00:18:21.960
Wait! Stop!

00:18:21.960 --> 00:18:23.710
Dear Vanitas!

00:18:27.540 --> 00:18:29.670
Pardon me!

00:18:48.060 --> 00:18:50.570
Pleased to meet you, Roland!

00:18:50.570 --> 00:18:52.070
My name is Noé.

00:18:52.070 --> 00:18:56.030
I came here with Vanitas to
investigate an incident of interest.

00:18:56.030 --> 00:18:59.780
Noé, you fool.
Why are you introducing yourself?

00:18:59.780 --> 00:19:05.750
First, please allow me to apologize
for entering your domain without leave.

00:19:05.750 --> 00:19:10.130
However, I swear we did not slay
the men we took these clothes from,

00:19:10.130 --> 00:19:12.670
nor did we harm them more than needed.

00:19:12.670 --> 00:19:18.140
So, please! Will you not
hear what we have to say?!

00:19:18.140 --> 00:19:21.390
What is wrong with you?

00:19:21.390 --> 00:19:22.930
Captain!

00:19:24.180 --> 00:19:27.060
Dr. Moreau yet lives!

00:19:29.480 --> 00:19:32.480
Now, listen to what we have to say.

00:19:34.070 --> 00:19:36.660
That <i>is </i>shocking news.

00:19:36.660 --> 00:19:42.950
We cast out Dr. Moreau,
yet he's been operating under our noses?

00:19:42.950 --> 00:19:46.120
And that's why vampires
are being abducted?

00:19:46.120 --> 00:19:47.790
It's just a tall tale!

00:19:47.790 --> 00:19:48.920
Is it not, Captain?

00:19:48.920 --> 00:19:52.550
I didn't want to explain about myself.

00:19:49.380 --> 00:19:52.420
No, it actually makes sense.

00:19:52.420 --> 00:19:55.220
There are no inconsistencies
in Vanitas's story.

00:19:52.550 --> 00:19:53.510
Why you...!

00:19:53.510 --> 00:19:56.380
I could've been killed
if things went south.

00:19:55.220 --> 00:19:56.380
But...

00:19:56.380 --> 00:19:59.260
And what you just did?!
Were you trying to kill me?

00:19:59.260 --> 00:20:02.390
What? I held back to make sure
you didn't break anything.

00:20:02.390 --> 00:20:04.640
That's not the issue!

00:20:04.640 --> 00:20:07.890
So are you really a vampire?

00:20:07.890 --> 00:20:08.810
What?

00:20:08.810 --> 00:20:13.440
Oh, it's merely, you're unlike
any vampire I've met before.

00:20:13.440 --> 00:20:14.820
Obviously.

00:20:14.820 --> 00:20:20.370
The Chasseurs only hunt the violent ones
who go rampaging through the human world.

00:20:20.370 --> 00:20:23.990
I see. That explains it.

00:20:23.990 --> 00:20:29.120
How interesting.
This is a truly intriguing find!

00:20:29.120 --> 00:20:30.750
I've made up my mind!

00:20:30.750 --> 00:20:34.090
My Dear Noé, let us be friends!

00:20:34.090 --> 00:20:37.130
I want to learn everything about you!

00:20:37.130 --> 00:20:39.010
Huh?!

00:20:39.010 --> 00:20:40.890
Gladly!

00:20:42.220 --> 00:20:44.510
That settles it.

00:20:44.510 --> 00:20:47.270
I shall join you!

00:20:47.270 --> 00:20:50.810
Wh-Wh-What has gotten into you, Captain?!

00:20:50.810 --> 00:20:56.480
What? That matter concerning Moreau is
something the Chasseurs must deal with.

00:20:56.480 --> 00:20:57.690
We must tell our superiors--

00:20:57.690 --> 00:21:01.870
I'd rather die than team up with you!
Don't you dare follow us!

00:21:01.870 --> 00:21:06.490
What a relief. He understood
once we explained the situation.

00:21:06.490 --> 00:21:09.160
He really did understand!

00:21:09.160 --> 00:21:11.670
But that begs the question...

00:21:11.670 --> 00:21:16.670
Why didn't you explain why
you're here in the first place?

00:21:29.810 --> 00:21:31.270
Vanitas.

00:21:31.270 --> 00:21:33.190
We're here.

00:21:33.190 --> 00:21:34.810
This is it.

00:21:43.280 --> 00:21:46.740
Welcome! Or should I say, welcome home!

00:21:46.740 --> 00:21:50.500
My Number 69!

00:21:50.500 --> 00:21:54.330
Do you remember me?!
You remember me, don't you?!

00:21:54.330 --> 00:21:57.920
It's Dr. Moreau!

00:21:58.880 --> 00:22:00.800
Vanitas...

00:22:05.350 --> 00:22:08.350
Dr. Moreau!
